\newlabel{sec:ch4_PBM-eg}{{4.5}{94}{Illustrative examples}{section.4.5}{}}
\newlabel{sec:ch4_PBM-eg@cref}{{[section][5][4]4.5}{[1][94][]94}{}{}{}}
\new@label@record{__tag_graphic.21}{{xpos}{8526659}{ypos}{30743268}{abspage}{115}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces  If given a trine state, each with equal probability, we have $\mathcal  {P}_{\mathrm  {Best}}=\mathcal  {P}_{\mathrm  {PGM}}=2/3$, with $\mathcal  {P}_{\text  {Random}}=1/3$ being the blind-guessing probability, and $\mathcal  {P}_{\mathrm  {PBM}}=1/6$ approximating $\mathcal  {P}_{\mathrm  {Worst}}=0$. The pretty good measurement is given by the POVM $G_i=\frac  {2}{3}| \psi _i \rangle \langle \psi _i |$; the pretty bad measurement is given by the POVM $B_i=\frac  {1}{3}\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{j\neq  i}| \psi _j \rangle \langle \psi _j |$; and the worst measurement is given by $W_i=\frac  {2}{3}| \psi _i^{\perp } \rangle \langle \psi _i^{\perp } |$, where $| \psi _i^{\perp } \rangle \langle \psi _i^{\perp } |$ is a $\pi /2$ rotation of $\ket {\psi _i}$. }}{95}{figure.caption.97}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch4_PBM-trine}{{4.1}{95}{If given a trine state, each with equal probability, we have $\Pbest =\PPGM =2/3$, with $\mathcal {P}_{\text {Random}}=1/3$ being the blind-guessing probability, and $\PPBM =1/6$ approximating $\Pworst =0$. The pretty good measurement is given by the POVM $G_i=\frac {2}{3}\kb {\psi _i}$; the pretty bad measurement is given by the POVM $B_i=\frac {1}{3}\sum _{j\neq i}\kb {\psi _j}$; and the worst measurement is given by $W_i=\frac {2}{3}\kb {\psi _i^{\perp }}$, where $\kb {\psi _i^{\perp }}$ is a $\pi /2$ rotation of $\ket {\psi _i}$}{figure.caption.97}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ch4_PBM-trine@cref}{{[figure][1][4]4.1}{[1][94][]95}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{eq:ch4_PBM-allthesame}{{4.27}{95}{Illustrative examples}{equation.4.27}{}}
\newlabel{eq:ch4_PBM-allthesame@cref}{{[equation][27][4]4.27}{[1][95][]95}{}{}{}}
